---
title: Lentil Chilli Non Carne
servings: 4
course: Main
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
prep time: 15m
cook time: 55m
cuisine: Mexican
---

Put the @puy or green lentils{100%g} in a pan of cold water and bring to the boil. Simmer for ~{20%minutes}, not allowing them to boil dry. They should be almost cooked after this time.

Heat the @sunflower oil{15%ml} in a #deep frying pan{} and sauté the @onion{1}(chopped), @garlic{2%cloves}(crushed), @carrot{1}(grated) and @parsnip{1}(peeled and grated) for ~{10%minutes}.

Add the @red chilli{1}(deseeded and finely chopped, or 2 tsp dried chilli flakes), @ground coriander{0.5%tsp} and @ground cumin{0.5%tsp}. Cook for ~{2%minutes}.

Add the @chopped tomatoes{1%tin × 400 g} to the frying pan with the @tomato purée{15%ml}, @balsamic vinegar{15%ml} and @vegetable stock cube{1}. Mix well.

Add the lentils and stir well. Cover and simmer on a low heat for ~{15%minutes}.

Add the @red kidney beans{200%g}(rinsed and drained) and heat through. Finally add the @coriander leaves{handful}(roughly chopped).

Serve with brown rice and a garnish of natural yoghurt.